id: pm-glossary-h5rj
title: "Owner: approve publication and certify additional providers"
description: "Owner-approved public repository, privacy and reviewer evidence, trusted publishing and provider conformance remain external gates. Upstream pm-cli issues 1399 1587 1588 own backend ports."
type: Feature
status: open
priority: 2
tags[4]: sdk-gap,"upstream:pm-cli#1399","upstream:pm-cli#1587","upstream:pm-cli#1588"
created_at: "2026-11-05T10:29:56.441Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-05T12:34:33.434Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Public review and repository creation; OIDC configuration; PM_RELEASE_APPROVED explicitly enabled; each provider native CAS conformance receipt
parent: pm-glossary-gjws
comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-05T10:52:24.246Z",codex-agent,"Verified upstream issues 1399, 1587 and 1588 remain open. Installed public SDK exposes PmClient.readItemRevision(id), withExpectedItemRevisions(expectations, operation) and a root-oriented directory client. The portable glossary kernel accepts an authorized injected port, but arbitrary-provider production certification requires separate host-owned capability and conformance evidence. Publication remains disabled until owner approval."
  "2026-11-05T12:34:33.433Z",codex-agent,"Provider evidence is limited to the directory host and injected contracts backed by actual native SDK trackers. There is no authoritative in-memory or database provider certification in this delivery. PmClientOptions exposes cwd, pmRoot, author and noExtensions, with no backend-port constructor; open upstream 1399, 1587 and 1588 own that missing native abstraction and conformance. Pure in-process resolution and capability-negative refusals remain available without fabricating an SDK storage implementation."
